  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing The Visuals**\n\nOkay, I\'m now zeroing in on the user\'s request, focusing intently on the visual components. I\'ve thoroughly absorbed the user prompt and the supplied mockups and HTML designs. My aim is to extract the essence of the desired app appearance so that I can provide the design and layout specified. I\'m taking notes on how to best \"hotlink\" the images from the HTML, which is a key part of the specifications.\n\n\n**Analyzing Screen Concepts**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously breaking down the visual elements outlined for the \"PhishGuard SOC COMMAND CENTER\" and the \"PhishGuard NEURAL URL SCANNER.\" I\'m now cataloging all the components, noting how the data should be displayed across the two screens. I\'m focusing on the KPIs, charts, live feeds, interactive modules, and the layout for each screen so I can offer suitable options.\n\n\n**Examining Forensic Details**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the forensic aspects outlined for the \"PhishGuard TELEMETRY HISTORY\" screen, specifically the level of detail provided for each record. I\'m focusing on the interaction with the forensic modal and will determine how to structure the detailed data presentation, including the risk scores, tags, and URL syntax highlighting. I\'m also considering the implications of batch actions like Quarantine and Export CSV.\n\n\n**Defining AI Interaction**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the \"PhishGuard SENTINEL AI ASSISTANT\" screen, focusing on the multimodal input dock and the voice-active mode toggle. I\'m carefully considering how to integrate the animated voice waveform orb and equalizer bars with the chat stream, which will include the Sentinel briefing, analyst queries, and the AI\'s diagnostic breakdown. I\'m also planning the tactical analysis prompts and the implementation of the mitigation recommendations, including the execute sinkhole and SIEM ticket options. Finally, I have reviewed the config settings.\n\n\n**Clarifying API Usage**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the use of the Gemini API. The current plan includes it for the Sentinel AI Assistant, which will analyze URLs and answer cyber intelligence questions. I\'m investigating the potential for a full-stack architecture, as per the guidelines, which will involve creating server-side API routes to secure the API key. I am checking the specifications to confirm that a backend is actually requested.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 286828446
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
