  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Font Resources**\n\nOkay, I\'m digging into the HTML to identify the font resources being used. So far, I\'ve located a couple of font links, specifically pointing to Google Fonts. I\'ve noted the families and weights specified, which are `Plus Jakarta Sans` and `JetBrains Mono`. This information is important for styling the page. Next I\'ll start processing these.\n\n\n**Identifying External Resources**\n\nI\'ve got the image resources mapped out now, specifically the PhishGuard logo and the profile avatar, and noted the Googleusercontent links. I\'m also now analyzing the custom colors and theming, as indicated in the prompt, with the design system specifications. I\'m building this all in a structured format now to ensure I don\'t miss anything.\n\n\n**Mapping Color Definitions**\n\nI\'ve just finished compiling the color definitions for the design system. I\'ve got a comprehensive list now, including the hex codes for each color variant, from `surface` to `on-error-container`. This is a pretty detailed palette. I\'m noting the roles each color plays in the design.\n\n\n**Reviewing Application Screens**\n\nI\'m now diving into the different application screens provided in the user\'s prompt. I\'ve started breaking down the \"SOC\" view, taking note of its key components, such as the command center, threat engine status, and quick scan button. I am identifying the KPIs, risk telemetry donut chart, and live intercept feed with risk scores. I\'m focusing on their layout and functionality.\n\n\n**Detailing Intercepted Data**\n\nI\'m currently documenting the data intercepted by the Neural URL Scanner. This includes scores, payloads, and timestamps from the live intercept feed. I\'ve also focused on the interactive SOC Defense Manual modules, and how they link to playbooks. Now, I\'m examining the `scan` view to record the user interactions and displayed data, like the URL input, verdict banners, and threat assessment dial. I\'m focusing on the individual risk indicators.\n\n\n**Examining Feature Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing the deep URL feature matrix, focusing on the 6-card grid and its data points like URL length and HTTPS certificate age. Then, I\'m analyzing the brand protection matrix, seeing the high similarity to Wells Fargo, and also taking note of the TLS/SSL state inspection. Finally, I\'ve started examining the remediation tactical buttons, like quarantine and block, and the export STIX IOC.\n\n\n**Defining Threat Records**\n\nI\'m now detailing the telemetry records list within the system. I am carefully documenting each element, including the checkbox selection, status pills indicating criticality, risk scores, URL display with syntax highlighting, threat breakdown, metadata, and the associated buttons for forensics and deletion. I\'m also noting the details of the sticky batch selection footer, with options for selecting, bulk actions, and exports. Finally, I\'m documenting the Forensics Modal Drawer overlay, the data, and the interactions associated with the forensic detail.\n\n\n\n**Defining Feature Integration**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on those advanced features! I\'m documenting the exfiltration signatures and associated mitigation recommendations, particularly those \"EXECUTE SINKHOLE\" and \"SHARE SIEM TICKET\" actions. I\'ve also noted the tactical analysis prompts, and am now turning my attention to the interactive chat capabilities, including the multimodal dock features, with the goal of analyzing the potential for expert responses. Finally, I\'ve started examining the config settings for the SOC radar and heuristic engine.\n\n\n**Verifying Styling Implementation**\n\nI\'m now diving into the styling implementation. I\'ve confirmed `@tailwindcss/vite` is in `vite.config.ts` and `@import \"tailwindcss\";` in `src/index.css`. My immediate goal is to make sure the Tailwind CSS classes and custom color variables, such as `bg-surface-container` and `text-on-surface`, are working correctly. I\'m exploring defining custom theme colors, either using the `@theme` directive in `src/index.css` or within the Tailwind configuration, and plan to test those now!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 197086187
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
