  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Exploring Tailwind\'s Theme Syntax**\n\nI\'ve been looking at how Tailwind CSS v4 introduces the `@theme` directive, which enables direct definition of theme tokens within `src/index.css`. This is an interesting change, allowing for a more straightforward way to manage and customize themes within a project\'s core styles.\n\n\n**Defining Theme Colors**\n\nI\'ve been mapping out specific color variables. I\'m focusing on a detailed palette, including primary, secondary, and tertiary colors with their corresponding containers and variants. I\'m also ensuring comprehensive coverage for surface colors. The aim is a full set of variables for consistent theming.\n\n\n**Incorporating Fixed Color Variables**\n\nI\'m now integrating fixed color variables into the theme. I\'ve defined error container colors, on-error variants, and fixed primary, secondary, and tertiary colors. This addition provides a strong foundation for consistent UI elements.\n\nI am also considering font variables, defining sizes and families. This ensures uniformity.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 827080201
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
