    thinking: "**Designing Screen 4**\n\nI\'m now focused on building Screen 4, specifically `src/components/SentinelAiAssistant.tsx`. I\'ve outlined the core elements: an AI Sentinel Status Header, complete with a mode switcher. This includes a header with a \"psychology\" icon in a `bg-surface-container-highest` background and a cool glowing halo. The title will be \"Sentinel AI Advisor.\"\n\n\n**Refining Screen 4 Detail**\n\nI\'ve been refining the elements of Screen 4. I\'ve added a subtitle \"PhishShield Engine \342\200\242 Real-time Threat Intel\" and a mute/unmute audio button. I\'m focusing on the Interactive Voice Waveform Orb Diagnostic Box, with atmospheric radial backdrops and pulsing radar ripples, along with an active listening button. I\'m also including SVG kinetic orbit particles, live telemetry frequency bars, and text indicating that I\'m listening. Finally, I\'ve added a conversational analytical timeline stream.\n\n\n**Analyzing Threat Intel**\n\nI\'ve just added a new threat intel report to the assistant, highlighting a suspicious domain, `wellsfarg0-verify.com`, and a DICT report with a 99.8% confidence rating. The classification details its homoglyph substitution, its zero-day age, and its exfiltration signature. The Sentinel\'s mitigation recommendation is to immediately sinkhole the domain and force OAuth session revocation. I\'ve designed tactical buttons to Execute Sinkhole and Share SIEM Ticket. I\'ve also added some quick prompt chips related to punycode attacks and OAuth, alongside DKIM/DMARC analysis and YARA rule generation. Finally, I\'ve started the multimodal chat and voice input dock with all the appropriate elements, with a radiant pulsing aura for voice and a violet send button.\n\n\n"
