  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 2
    session_summary: "### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n*   **UI Redesign (Sidebar Navigation):**\n    *   **Status:** IMPLEMENTATION\n    *   **Request:** Remove the bottom navigation bar completely. Implement a fixed professional vertical sidebar on the left for all navigation (Dashboard, URL Scanner, Scan History, AI Security Chatbot, Security Tips, Settings).\n    *   **Current State:** `BottomNav.tsx` has been deleted. `Sidebar.tsx` has been created. The next step is to integrate the `Sidebar` into `App.tsx` and adjust the layout to a flex container.\n*   **Aesthetic & Layout Overhaul:**\n    *   **Status:** IMPLEMENTATION\n    *   **Request:** Improve the overall dashboard layout to look like a premium modern cybersecurity SaaS application.\n    *   **Specifics:** Use a dark charcoal background; Purple/Violet (AI), Teal/Cyan (Tech), Green (Safe), Orange (Suspicious), Red (Phishing) accents.\n    *   **Current State:** `SocCommandCenter.tsx` has been redesigned with the new aesthetic. `SecurityTipsView.tsx` has been created.\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n\n*   **Navigation Rules:** \"Remove the entire bottom navigation bar completely.\" \"Navigation must exist ONLY in the LEFT SIDEBAR.\" \"The main dashboard content must occupy the entire area to the RIGHT of the sidebar.\" \"Do not place any duplicate navigation, tabs, or bottom menu on desktop.\"\n*   **Design Preferences:** \"Avoid making blue the dominant color.\"\n*   **Color Palette:** \"Dark charcoal background, Purple/Violet accents for AI, Teal/Cyan accents for technology, Green for safe websites, Orange for suspicious websites, Red for phishing threats.\"\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n\n*   **Structural Discovery:** Mapped the existing `App.tsx` state management (`currentTab`) and component architecture.\n*   **Implementation:**\n    *   **Types:** Updated `NavTab` in `/src/types.ts` to include the new navigation items (`dashboard`, `scanner`, `history`, `chatbot`, `tips`, `settings`).\n    *   **Navigation:** Deleted `/src/components/BottomNav.tsx`.\n    *   **Sidebar:** Created `/src/components/Sidebar.tsx` with the requested links and layout.\n    *   **Dashboard:** Redesigned `/src/components/SocCommandCenter.tsx` to match the premium dark charcoal aesthetic and include new metrics.\n    *   **Security Tips:** Created `/src/components/SecurityTipsView.tsx` to handle the \'tips\' navigation tab.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n\n*   **Architecture:** The application is a React SPA using Vite, Tailwind CSS, and Lucide React.\n*   **Routing:** `App.tsx` manages the view state via `currentTab`.\n*   **Layout Constraint:** The current `App.tsx` structure is a vertical flex column. This must be changed to a horizontal flex row (Sidebar + Main content) to accommodate the new fixed sidebar.\n*   **Styling:** The project uses a custom Tailwind theme defined in `index.css`.\n*   **Dependencies:** The project uses `@google/genai`, `lucide-react`, and `motion`.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n\n*   **Edited/Created Files:**\n    *   `/src/types.ts`: Updated `NavTab` to include new sidebar routes.\n    *   `/src/components/Sidebar.tsx`: Created. Contains the fixed left sidebar navigation.\n    *   `/src/components/SocCommandCenter.tsx`: Redesigned to match the new UI requirements.\n    *   `/src/components/SecurityTipsView.tsx`: Created.\n    *   `/src/components/BottomNav.tsx`: Deleted.\n*   **Viewed Files:**\n    *   `/src/App.tsx`: Essential for integrating the new `Sidebar` and updating the layout.\n    *   `/src/index.css`: Reference for color palette and theme variables.\n    *   `/src/data/mockData.ts`: Source for dashboard metrics and playbook content.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n*   **Current Work:** The application is currently in a transitional state where the `BottomNav` is removed, but the `Sidebar` has not yet been integrated into `App.tsx`.\n*   **Next Steps:**\n    1.  **Integrate `Sidebar`:** Modify `/src/App.tsx` to import and render the `Sidebar` component.\n    2.  **Update Layout:** Change the main wrapper in `/src/App.tsx` to a `flex flex-row` layout so the sidebar sits on the left and the main content fills the remaining space.\n    3.  **Update Routing:** Ensure `App.tsx` handles the new `NavTab` values (e.g., mapping \'dashboard\' to `SocCommandCenter`, \'tips\' to `SecurityTipsView`).\n    4.  **Cleanup:** Remove any redundant imports or code from `App.tsx` related to the old `BottomNav`.\n    5.  **Verify:** Ensure the responsive design (mobile drawer) in `Sidebar.tsx` works as expected."
    included_step_index_start: 61
    included_step_index_end: 106
    conversation_log_uris: "file:///.aistudio/artifacts/brain/d89cc6b6-d2f2-4875-9c9e-87b23d4e6d1e/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl"
    user_requests: "User prompt: Build me an app with screens that look like this. You can hotlink images from the HTML\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport fs from \'fs\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig, Plugin} from \'vite\';\n\n// LINT.IfChange(aistudio_media_plugin)\nfunction aistudioMediaPlugin(): Plugin {\n  return {\n    name: \'vite-plugin-aistudio-media\',\n    configureServer(server) {\n      server.middlewares.use((req, res, next) => {\n        if (req.url && req.url.startsWith(\'/assets/aistudio/\')) {\n          const rawPath = req.url.split(\'?\')[0].split(\'#\')[0];\n          try {\n            const decodedPath = decodeURIComponent(rawPath);\n            const relativePath = decodedPath.replace(/^\\//, \'\');\n            const aistudioDir = path.resolve(\n              __dirname,\n              \'public\',\n              \'assets\',\n              \'aistudio\',\n            );\n            const filePath = path.resolve(__dirname, \'public\', relativePath);\n            if (\n              filePath.startsWith(aistudioDir + path.sep) &&\n              fs.existsSync(filePath) &&\n              fs.statSync(filePath).isFile()\n            ) {\n              const ext = path.extname(filePath).toLowerCase();\n              const mimeMap: Record<string, string> = {\n                \'.jpg\': \'image/jpeg\',\n                \'.jpeg\': \'image/jpeg\',\n                \'.png\': \'image/png\',\n                \'.gif\': \'image/gif\',\n                \'.webp\': \'image/webp\',\n                \'.svg\': \'image/svg+xml\',\n                \'.bmp\': \'image/bmp\',\n                \'.ico\': \'image/x-icon\',\n                \'.mp4\': \'video/mp4\',\n                \'.webm\': \'video/webm\',\n                \'.ogv\': \'video/ogg\',\n                \'.mp3\': \'audio/mpeg\',\n                \'.wav\': \'audio/wav\',\n                \'.ogg\': \'audio/ogg\',\n                \'.pdf\': \'application/pdf\',\n              };\n              res.setHeader(\n                \'Content-Type\',\n                mimeMap[ext] || \'application/octet-stream\',\n              );\n              res.setHeader(\'Cache-Control\', \'no-cache\');\n              fs.createReadStream(filePath).pipe(res);\n              return;\n            }\n          } catch {\n            // Fall through if URI decoding or file access fails\n          }\n        }\n        next();\n      });\n    },\n  };\n}\n// LINT.ThenChange(//depot/google3/java/com/google/alkali/boq/makersuite/applet_dev_service/templates/initializers/react_theme/vite.config.ts:aistudio_media_plugin)\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss(), aistudioMediaPlugin()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    user_requests: "Build me an app with screens that look like this. You can hotlink images from the HTML"
    user_requests: "Redesign the existing PhishGuard AI dashboard UI without changing the existing functionality.\n\nCRITICAL FIX:\n\nRemove the entire bottom navigation bar completely.\n\nThe bottom navigation currently contains duplicate menu items such as:\n- SOC / Dashboard\n- Scan\n- Logs / Scan History\n- Sentinel / AI Assistant\n- Config / Settings\n\nDELETE this bottom navigation completely.\n\nNavigation must exist ONLY in the LEFT SIDEBAR.\n\nKeep a fixed professional vertical sidebar on the left side of the desktop layout.\n\nThe sidebar should contain:\n- Dashboard\n- URL Scanner\n- Scan History\n- AI Security Chatbot\n- Security Tips\n- Settings\n\nThe main dashboard content must occupy the entire area to the RIGHT of the sidebar.\n\nDo not place any duplicate navigation, tabs, or bottom menu on desktop.\n\nImprove the overall dashboard layout to look like a premium modern cybersecurity SaaS application.\n\nUse:\n- Dark charcoal background\n- Purple/Violet accents for AI\n- Teal/Cyan accents for technology\n- Green for safe websites\n- Orange for suspicious websites\n- Red for phishing threats\n\nAvoid making blue the dominant color.\n\nImprove spacing, alignment, card hierarchy, typography, and visual balance.\n\nCreate a clean dashboard with:\n- Top header\n- Scan URL button\n- Total Scans\n- Safe Websites\n- Suspicious Websites\n- Phishing Websites\n- Risk Analytics chart\n- Recent Scan Activity\n- AI-powered protection section\n- Security Tips section\n\nMake the desktop UI spacious and professional.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThere must be NO bottom navigation bar.\nNavigation should appear ONLY in the left sidebar."
  }
}
